course: dictionary
lesson: 13460
title: Feeling humiliated
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When someone feels humiliated, they feel very ashamed and embarrassed, as if they look foolish in front of other people. The clues in a sentence show you this meaning. «Mia felt humiliated when she tripped on the stage in front of the whole school.» Tripping is an accident, and the words «in front of the whole school» tell you she felt foolish in front of everyone. Humiliated means very ashamed and embarrassed.
explain: Humiliate is the verb, and humiliated is its past form. Someone can humiliate you, so you can be humiliated by what another person does. «The bully tried to humiliate Sam by sharing an embarrassing photo.» Here the bully is doing the humiliating, and Sam is the one who feels ashamed.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Mia felt very ashamed and embarrassed» still make sense? Yes, so you have it right. Humiliated is a strong, painful word, so it is used for serious hurt, not for a small mistake that you laugh off.
fact: Humiliated means feeling very ashamed and embarrassed, as if you look foolish in front of others.
fact: Humiliate means to make someone feel very ashamed and foolish, especially in public.
fact: «Humiliated» is the past form of «humiliate»: humiliate, humiliates, humiliated, humiliating.
fact: Phrases to know: feel humiliated, be humiliated in front of others, publicly humiliated.
fact: Humiliating others is wrong, and if a friend feels humiliated, you can support them by being kind.
exercise: «Mia felt humiliated when she tripped on the stage in front of the whole school.» What does humiliated mean here? | Pleased and proud | Angry with the stage | Tired and sleepy | *Very ashamed and embarrassed
exercise: «The bully tried to humiliate Sam by sharing an embarrassing photo.» What is the bully trying to do? | Take a photo of the sky | *Make Sam feel ashamed and foolish | Help Sam with his homework
exercise: Which word in this sentence is the past form of humiliate? «Ben humiliated his rival, then said sorry.» | *humiliated | Ben | sorry | rival
test: «Nobody should be humiliated for making a mistake.» What should you do if a friend feels humiliated? | *Support them and be kind to them | Share a photo of them with everyone | Laugh at them so they feel better
test: Which phrase means someone was shamed in front of other people? | *Publicly humiliated | Happily surprised | Quietly sleeping | Very hungry
exam: «After the bully shared his photo, Kai felt so humiliated that he hid in the library all day.» What does this sentence show? | Humiliating others is fun and harmless | Photos are always funny | Kai really liked the library | *Humiliating others hurts them deeply, so it is wrong
